<title>JAPAN: Japan May green coffee imports up 8.79 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May green coffee imports up 8.79 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports during May totalled 33,907 tonnes, up 8.79 percent from the same month a year ealier, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 140 tonnes in May against 157 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of green coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   May 97	   Apr 97	   May 96</p>
<p> Total	  33,907	    31,059	   31,167</p>
<p> Brazil	  7,784	     7,111	    5,469</p>
<p> Colombia	4,789	     5,162	    7,131</p>
<p> Indonesia     6,407	     5,312	    5,254</p>
<p> Honduras	1,455	     1,664	    1,181</p>
<p> Guatemala     2,047	     2,494	    2,853</p>
<p> Vietnam	 1,957	     2,572	    2,039</p>
<p> Mexico	  1,674	     1,865	    1,184</p>
<p> Tanzania	1,201		 816		766</p>
<p> Ethiopia	2,618	     1,506	    1,630</p>
<p>Total green coffee imports in the first five months of 1997 were 150,750 tonnes against 124,360 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     May 97	  Apr 97	   May 96</p>
<p> Total	     140		134	     157</p>
<p>Cumulative roasted coffee imports in the first five months of 1997 were 981 tonnes against 867 tonnes the year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
